arc number B1933 is the one main reserved for it (M38).

THE FOUNDATION, version 1.69, written by its own script (verification/write_version_1_69.py, which names each line it
replaces by its whole old text and stops if one is not there once):
  - the m000 row of the table of frames (it read "never computed" in all four): F-FC closed, b1 = 1 and cusp rank 1 at
    every level n = 1 to 8 (B1926, verifying the web seat's W-C8 part 2a, harvest rows 1755 and 1768); F-CI no sector
    module at any odd level, every class free on the scar over the characters twisted by the orientation, the twisted
    classes the double cover's matter seen from below (B1926 and its addendum, three codes), whether they count a
    stated choice (B1926); F-HE and F-AP never computed, offered to the SM seat (its page, M28);
  - "Computed nowhere yet": the m000 entry narrowed to F-HE and F-AP; the harmonic frame's counts outside m004's levels
    marked as computed once by agy-exp's X-NEVER on eight chiral word states (harvest row 1797), its second computation
    owed, and kept on the list (main's M36). X-NEVER's other first computations are in agy-exp's lane, read through
    main's mask; each is marked when main gives which item it computed.
  - the log's entry above 1.68's; the version's line at 1.69. No other item or status changes.
  - the foundation is on the public face, so its new text uses none of the record's inner words: the web seat's
    computation is "an independent sealed computation", X-NEVER "an independent computation", the offer "offered for
    computation"; the harvest rows it cites name them. The public-face gate holds GENESIS's counts unchanged.

THE ARC B1933: its page (the answer first, Seen first with its sweep, Literature), a PROCESS row in the representation
triage (its own page is the synthesis surface, as for the earlier versions), its verdict file (PROVED: the foundation's statement;
no computation made here), and its lock: the page at 1.69, each new cell's words found in its source (B1926's page and
verdict line, the harvest rows), the script giving the page again from it with this version taken back; planted, the old
row put back and the computed-once mark taken off, each refused.

B1930'S LOCK MENDED, with a dated docstring: it held the page's being at 1.68; it now takes each later version back by
that version's own lock and holds 1.68 there, as B1904's lock holds "the version only moves forward". The foundation's
locks: 13 passed (B1930, B1933, B1904), and 164 of the tests that read the foundation pass.

